# Local storage and sync (JPL)

## Topology
- One server; thousands of MAUI clients.
- League Admin feature data uses local SQLite. After login, do not call feature APIs outside explicit Sync operations.
- League User, SuperAdmin, GroundOwner, and Guest feature data uses live APIs and must not be persisted as local feature cache data.

## League Admin
- Use local SQLite for reads and writes in every feature, including cold start; never fall back to feature APIs.
- Only the bound home league (`AuthSession.LeagueId`) may push and pull via Sync.
- Home-league writes queue durably for Sync; keep match and nets live scoring in `LiveOutbox`.
- Login is server authenticated. Avoid standalone `/api/auth/me` requests after login; validate the session through Sync.
- The HTTP handler must block every League Admin feature request except explicit Sync routes. Live feed/list routes are not an exception.

## Other roles
- Read and write league feature data through live APIs; do not use local feature caches or local business-data outboxes.
- Authentication state and ephemeral UI preferences are not feature data.

## Sync correctness
- Keep SQLite Guid TEXT lowercase; startup normalizes casing so EF lookups never miss rows and cache inserts never hit duplicate PKs.
- Push uses idempotency keys and server receipts so retries are safe.
- Pull uses per-league cursors; protected local work must defer remote rows without losing replayable copies.
- Conflicts must be resolvable (accept server / keep local), never terminal-only.
- Do not hard-gate sync on `Connectivity.NetworkAccess`. Attempt HTTP and treat transport failures as offline.
- Do not sync incomplete match/nets scoring through the completed-match outbox (`LiveOutbox` only).
- Do not globally block unrelated entity types behind one failed parent row.
- Prune only after Completed; never delete Pending/Failed/InFlight rows.
- Do not put ImagePath binaries through the change-feed payload.
- Manual and automatic full Sync are only for League Admin's home league.

Use `LeagueSyncPolicy.UsesLocalStorage(session)` for League Admin feature data. Use `LeagueSyncPolicy.AllowsLocalOfflineSync(session, selectedLeagueId)` only for home-league Sync and outbox paths.
